Z||000000||KRMFiero||06-27-2001||09:48 AM||||I know since 1 T-3 (T-Birt Turbo) would probley spool up to fast or something on the V-8 so what about two? If I run one of each side of the V (4 cylinders per turbo) then run the High Pressure air together and then into the intake  would this work? I only want about 5-7 psi of boost max, will this be to much? I have very little room but I might be able to sqeese two turbos in. What should I change before I install turbo(s)?<BR>I plan on:<BR>New Oilcooler and Lines<BR>Dropping Oil Pan to clean out.<P>If the T-3's wont work what would be a better turbo for me (I want to try to stay with a single one and i only want 5-7psi max) and what kind of car/truck can i get it out of?<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 Project<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>       <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> <BR>AOL: Physcokyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||06-27-2001||04:37 PM||||How 'bout new head gaskets? I'd be afraid to turbo a Caddy 4.x. Seriously, I'd pull the heads, precisely check the height of all the boreliners, and put it back together with a set of good quality (Felpro) head gaskets. Plan on dropping about $200 for a full gasket set for that engine. <BR> I don't have first hand experience, but they have been known to have high head gasket failure rates. <BR> Two small turbos would probably fit nicely above the trans. Do you have Seville or Deville manifolds?<P>My Cadero page is up <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm</A> <P>Jon||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||06-27-2001||05:29 PM||||1989 Seville||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||06-27-2001||05:29 PM||||i'd have to wait till i got home to tell you the exact issue, but there is an article like that in muscle mustangs and fast fords mag. they take two junkyard 2.3 ford turbos and an intercooler from a semi (from a semi junkyard) and put them on a 302. displacement wise it seems like it would work on a 4.9, maybe a 4.5 also. i know there would be lots of differences but it dose explore the idea. they did it for $1000 too. <p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||06-27-2001||06:41 PM||||I think that using the Seville manifolds will make it a little bit tougher to pipe the turbos in unless you put them way down low, one on each side. I'd imagine they need to be pretty close to the intake for best operation.  The Deville manifolds each have an outlet pointing up and out the back like a 2.8 Fiero. It seems like maybe they'd be a little easier to work with. But I've never done anything with a turbo. Are you planning on cutting out the trunk? Using Fiero exhaust system?||||reg||1
Z||000005||KRMFiero||06-27-2001||09:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>Are you planning on cutting out the trunk? Using Fiero exhaust system?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was thinking about cutting the trunk back about 4-5" or so to have some more room in the comparment and stuff but i am worryed about that support beam that goes accross...<P>I havent desided on exaust system yet, i was gonna get a Borla or Oclator and then just run the oulet of the turbos to that so it looks stock but im not sure if the 2" pipe will be big enough<BR>||||reg||1
